<title>USA: FGIC qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Guaranty Insurance Co said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following five municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--San Francisco Airports, Calif., $275 million revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--North Brandford, Conn., $9.6 million general obligation bonds.  </p>
<p>--Clark County, Nev., $7.2 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Metro Government of Nashville and Davidson Counties, Tenn., $96.135 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Grapevine, Texas, $9.785 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
